# What this repository does not track.
#
# The path carries the role. `models/`, `reports/` and `docs/` hold what is published;
# everything a run leaves behind lives under `var/`, including the Kaggle download, the
# frames derived from it, the MLflow store and the coverage database. No line here begins
# with `!`, because an exception means the line above ignored something that had to be
# kept, and that arbitration belongs to the tree rather than to this file. The version this
# replaces carried eight of them, five to re-include the three model files.

# Everything a run writes and no reader opens: logs, checkpoints, MLflow, TensorBoard,
# profiles, the coverage database and its HTML report. The only ignored directory.
var/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/

# Tool caches
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Secrets. `.env.example` is tracked and is not matched by this line: it is `.env` exactly,
# so keeping the example needs no exception.
.env
.streamlit/secrets.toml

# Editors and operating systems
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
